<title>FRANCE: Dass.Electronique in French air force deal.</title>
<headline>Dass.Electronique in French air force deal.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dassault Electronique said on Wednesday it has a contract for the mid-life update of the &quot;Barax&quot; electronic countermeasures (ECM) pods on Dassault Aviation Mirage F1 combat planes in the French air force. There are about 100 Mirage F1s in the fleet.</p>
<p>The contract involves using the latest technology to allow the aircraft to protect themselves against the new generation of threats, the company said in a statement. It gave no value for the contract.</p>
<p>The ECM suite, which has shown its operational effectiveness, will also be offered in export markets, it said.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
